  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the area $A$ bounded between the curve $x=2-{y}^{8}$, the $y$-axis, and the lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the area, we compute the corresponding definite integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{c}^{d}x(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-{y}^{8})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y\\,-\\,{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{8}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{1}\\,-\\,{\\frac{{y}^{9}}{9}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2(1-0)\\,-\\,(\\frac{1}{9}-0) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
